<task id="002" project="spaarkeai-compose-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Assemble the fidelity corpus as LFS fixtures (sample-docs + owner worst-offenders)</title>
    <phase>0 Gate</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New fixture files + a catalog markdown; no `.cs`/`.ts` implementation, no cutover. New-file creation with a defined contract — STANDARD.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical assembly + cataloguing against a fully-specified feature-coverage matrix; no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>W0a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps></deps>
    <tags>testing,fixtures,docx</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 day</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Assemble the R4 fidelity corpus as Git-LFS `.docx` fixtures. Copy the three owner sample documents from
    `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/sample-docs/` into a new fixtures directory
    `tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/` and author a `corpus-manifest.md` cataloguing each document's
    worst-offender OOXML features and the known defect it exercises. `.docx` is already LFS-tracked via
    `.gitattributes` (`*.docx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text`) — confirm the copied files land as LFS
    pointers, not raw binaries.

    THE THREE SAMPLE DOCS TO REGISTER (copy verbatim from `notes/sample-docs/`):
    (1) `PAT 109270W-1 - CLAIMS track changes vs US12470413 claims(206092900.1).docx` — the CIPO patent
        letter: THE Phase-0 spike/UAT document. Exercises the known interior-location HTTP 422, empty-paragraph
        drift (mammoth dropped 9 paragraphs, 48 vs 39), and pre-existing track-changes import.
    (2) `Engagement Letter.docx` — a formatted legal contract (letterhead, numbered clauses).
    (3) `01 - Test Matter Create Fields Only.docx` — the fields / content-controls (SDT) case.

    The manifest is a table with columns: filename, feature coverage (track changes / fields / SDT / tables /
    tabs / multi-level numbering / headers-footers / empty paragraphs / multi-section), and the known-defect
    it exercises. Include PLACEHOLDER rows for the owner-supplied worst-offenders that arrive during Phase 0
    (spec Unresolved Question — corpus documents). Do NOT invent owner documents; leave labelled placeholders.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Test-fixtures engineer who understands the R4 acceptance model: the byte-diff harness (task 004) and the
    hard-replace gate (task 006) both consume this corpus as their acceptance evidence base. Knows Git-LFS
    pointer semantics and OOXML feature vocabulary (w:ins/w:del, SDT/content controls, w:fldSimple, multi-level
    numbering, sectPr).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new `tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/` directory containing the three owner sample documents registered as
    Git-LFS `.docx` fixtures (LFS pointers, verified via `git lfs ls-files`), plus a `corpus-manifest.md`
    cataloguing each document's worst-offender feature coverage and the known defect it exercises, with clearly
    labelled placeholder rows for the owner-supplied worst-offenders that arrive later in Phase 0. The CIPO
    patent letter is flagged as THE Phase-0 spike/UAT document.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R4 is a hard-replace cutover with no A/B parallel-run; the Phase 0 proof gate (task 006) is the safety
      net, and the byte-diff harness (task 004) is its acceptance evidence — both need a fixed, versioned
      corpus (spec NFR-08, design §6 Phase 0). The three owner sample docs already exist under
      `notes/sample-docs/`; this task promotes them to first-class LFS fixtures under a stable test path and
      catalogues what each one stresses. The owner will supply additional redacted worst-offenders during
      Phase 0 (spec Unresolved Question: "Corpus documents — owner to supply the worst-offender set"), so the
      manifest carries placeholder rows now. `.docx` is already LFS-tracked in `.gitattributes`.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/PAT 109270W-1 - CLAIMS track changes vs US12470413 claims(206092900.1).docx — the CIPO patent letter (copy from notes/sample-docs/); THE Phase-0 spike/UAT doc</file>
      <file role="new">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/Engagement Letter.docx — formatted legal contract (copy from notes/sample-docs/)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/01 - Test Matter Create Fields Only.docx — fields / content-controls case (copy from notes/sample-docs/)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/corpus-manifest.md — the feature-coverage + known-defect catalog with owner-placeholder rows</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/sample-docs/ — source of the three documents to copy verbatim</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/as-built-inventory.md — the known R3 UAT failure surfaces (interior-location 422, empty-paragraph drift) each corpus doc must exercise</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-01, NFR-01, NFR-08, Unresolved Questions (corpus)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependencies — startable Phase-0 gate task; tasks 004 and 005 depend on THIS.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The three named sample documents MUST be copied verbatim from `notes/sample-docs/` into `tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/` and land as Git-LFS pointers (not raw binaries). Scope: verify with `git lfs ls-files` / `git check-attr filter`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-01 / NFR-01">The manifest MUST catalog each doc's feature coverage across at least: track changes, fields, SDT/content controls, tables, tabs, multi-level numbering, headers/footers, empty paragraphs, multi-section — and name the known defect each exercises. Scope: the CIPO doc is flagged as the interior-location-422 + empty-paragraph-drift case and THE Phase-0 spike/UAT doc.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / Unresolved Question">The manifest MUST include labelled placeholder rows for owner-supplied worst-offenders arriving during Phase 0. Scope: do NOT fabricate owner documents — placeholders only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT bloat the repo with un-LFS'd binaries. Scope: confirm `.gitattributes` `*.docx filter=lfs` applies to the new path before committing.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Git-LFS fixture registration; OOXML worst-offender feature vocabulary; R4 corpus acceptance model; R3 known UAT failure surfaces</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/as-built-inventory.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="LFS-tracked docx fixtures" location=".gitattributes">
        `*.docx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text` — copying a `.docx` under a tracked path auto-registers it as an LFS pointer; verify with `git lfs ls-files`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Known failure surfaces as acceptance targets" location="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/as-built-inventory.md">
        The R3 UAT failure surfaces (interior-location 422 via text-search, empty-paragraph drift 48→39, eTag-mismatch) — map each corpus doc to the defect(s) it exercises so the harness has a target.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: STANDARD / 📋 REASON / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS). Load spec §FR-01/NFR-01/NFR-08 + as-built-inventory known-failure surfaces.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Create the fixtures directory">Create `tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/`. Confirm `.gitattributes` `*.docx filter=lfs` covers this path (`git check-attr filter tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/x.docx`).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Copy the three sample docs">Copy the three named documents verbatim from `notes/sample-docs/` into the fixtures directory (preserve filenames exactly, including spaces + parentheses).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Verify LFS registration">Run `git add` + `git lfs ls-files` (or `git lfs status`) to confirm all three land as LFS pointers, not raw binaries.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Author the manifest">Write `corpus-manifest.md` with the feature-coverage + known-defect table for the three docs (CIPO flagged as THE Phase-0 spike/UAT doc), plus labelled placeholder rows for owner worst-offenders.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Close out">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 002 status to ✅. Record any deviation (e.g., an LFS-tracking surprise) in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A copied `.docx` does NOT land as an LFS pointer (raw binary staged) — STOP before committing; a mis-tracked multi-MB binary in git history is expensive to reverse. Surface the `.gitattributes` gap.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No corpus fixtures dir exists; the sample docs live only under `notes/sample-docs/` (not a test-consumable path). Verified via Glob of `tests/fixtures/`.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot extend an existing fixtures set — none targets Compose corpus round-trip. This creates the single canonical corpus path both task 004 (harness) and task 006 (gate) consume.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a fixed, versioned corpus, the NFR-01 byte-diff harness and the hard-replace gate (NFR-08) have no acceptance evidence — the cutover would proceed with no safety net.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="fixture">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/*.docx (3 LFS-tracked sample documents)</output>
    <output type="doc">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/corpus-manifest.md (feature-coverage + known-defect catalog with owner-placeholder rows)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">`tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/` contains the three named sample documents copied verbatim from `notes/sample-docs/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git lfs ls-files` shows all three `.docx` files as LFS pointers (no raw binary staged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`corpus-manifest.md` catalogs each doc across the required feature columns (track changes / fields / SDT / tables / tabs / multi-level numbering / headers-footers / empty paragraphs / multi-section) and names the known defect each exercises.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The CIPO patent letter is flagged in the manifest as THE Phase-0 spike/UAT doc and the interior-location-422 + empty-paragraph-drift case.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest includes clearly labelled placeholder rows for owner-supplied worst-offenders (none fabricated).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 002 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Owner supplies additional redacted worst-offenders during Phase 0 (spec Unresolved Question). The manifest's
    placeholder rows are the intake slots. Blocks the final NFR-01 acceptance bar, NOT Phase-0 start — the three
    seed docs are enough to stand up the harness (task 004) and the applier spike (task 005).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
